        <body>
            <div xml:id="d836">

                <pb facs="0816" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg718"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Baron Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 557.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I regret to find that your note of
                    January 15 last, in further reference to the case of the lynching of persons of
                    Italian origin at Tallulah, La., and with which you inclosed a report from the
                    acting consul at New Orleans, was, through an unaccountable oversight, not
                    acknowledged at the time of its receipt.</p>
                <p>Copy of your note, with its inclosure, was, however, immediately sent to the
                    governor of Louisiana with appropriate commendation to his excellency’s early
                    and attentive notice.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
